00:52:16.063 --> 00:52:17.855
Actual output from running it:

708
00:52:19.205 --> 00:52:20.122
On screen:

709
00:52:20.402 --> 00:52:43.805
500 mangoes, 2,000 buyers, hold TTL 300 ms, payment takes 50 to 450 ms, expiry sweeper. every 20 ms. unguarded CONFIRM (by id only): confirmed 801, confirm refused (hold expired, then refund) 0, turned away (none. available at TRY) 1199. holds:

710
00:52:44.085 --> 00:53:10.730
CONFIRMED 801, RELEASED 0, still HELD 0; units returned by the sweeper 301. conservation: available 0 + confirmed 801 = 801 (must be 500). guarded CONFIRM (status = HELD and not expired): confirmed 500, confirm refused (hold expired, then refund) 342, turned away (none. available at TRY) 1158. holds:

711
00:53:11.010 --> 00:53:30.189
CONFIRMED 500, RELEASED 342, still HELD 0; units returned by the sweeper 342. conservation: available 0 + confirmed 500 = 500 (must be 500). every refused confirm was released exactly once: yes.

712
00:53:33.039 --> 00:53:35.449
Unguarded confirm (by id only):

713
00:53:35.729 --> 00:53:38.823
801 confirmed for 500 mangoes.

714
00:53:39.103 --> 00:53:46.228
The sweeper had already released 301 expired holds and returned their units to stock, which other buyers took.

715
00:53:46.508 --> 00:53:49.793
Then the original buyers' late confirms also succeeded.

716
00:53:50.073 --> 00:53:53.807
That's oversold by 301, and there was no error anywhere.

717
00:53:54.087 --> 00:54:02.215
Guarded confirm: the confirm only succeeds for a hold that is HELD and not expired by the database's clock, in the same statement.

718
00:54:02.495 --> 00:54:13.076
Exactly 500 were confirmed, 342 late confirms were refused (the saga refunds them), and every refused hold was released exactly once.

719
00:54:14.426 --> 00:54:23.983
The design lever is the TTL: with 300 ms against 50 to 450 ms payments, 17 % of buyers were refunded.

720
00:54:24.263 --> 00:54:34.461
In production the TTL comes from the payment-time distribution (UPI approvals can take minutes), traded against how long unsold stock stays locked.

