929
01:05:24.697 --> 01:05:30.990
Holds: active holds, expirations versus confirmations, late confirms (refunds), sweeper lag.

930
01:05:31.270 --> 01:05:45.030
Reconciliation: a nightly job checks the §5 invariants across services (confirmed ⇔ captured ⇔ reserved; stock conservation; payments versus Razorpay settlement report) and reports mismatches.

931
01:05:45.310 --> 01:05:47.486
It's the safety net for everything above.

932
01:05:48.836 --> 01:05:49.775
Security.

933
01:05:50.055 --> 01:05:59.889
Idempotency keys must be scoped to the caller (customer + key, or service identity + key), so one tenant can't replay another's key to read its result.

934
01:06:00.169 --> 01:06:09.300
Compensations move money (refunds): they need the same authorization and audit trail as the forward path, and must not be triggerable from the outside.

935
