Part 7.

1000
01:09:12.472 --> 01:09:14.179
Anti-Patterns and Pitfalls.

1001
01:09:15.429 --> 01:09:17.861
1. @Transactional around remote calls.

1002
01:09:18.141 --> 01:09:18.951
Symptom:

1003
01:09:19.231 --> 01:09:22.645
Charged-without-order, stuck stock (§1.1).

1004
01:09:22.925 --> 01:09:25.805
The annotation only covers the local connection.

1005
01:09:26.085 --> 01:09:26.810
Fix:

1006
01:09:27.090 --> 01:09:30.887
Local transactions + saga + idempotent participants.

1007
01:09:31.167 --> 01:09:31.871
2.

1008
01:09:32.151 --> 01:09:34.519
Publishing events after commit (dual write).

1009
01:09:35.869 --> 01:09:42.717
Here is the Java code. before: a crash or broker outage between these two lines loses the event (L1:

1010
01:09:42.997 --> 01:09:52.917
1,696 of 100,000). after: the event is a row in the same transaction; the relay publishes it (at least once).

1011
01:09:55.767 --> 01:09:56.514
3.

1012
01:09:56.794 --> 01:09:58.650
Consumers that aren't idempotent.

1013
01:09:58.930 --> 01:09:59.741
Symptom:

1014
01:10:00.021 --> 01:10:04.202
Double reservations and double emails after redeliveries (L2:

1015
01:10:04.482 --> 01:10:06.082
403 extra).

1016
01:10:06.362 --> 01:10:07.087
Fix:

1017
01:10:07.367 --> 01:10:12.338
Inbox table or natural idempotency, in the same transaction as the effect.

1018
01:10:12.618 --> 01:10:13.322
4.

1019
01:10:13.602 --> 01:10:15.159
Compensating on a timeout.

1020
01:10:15.439 --> 01:10:16.250
Symptom:

1021
01:10:16.530 --> 01:10:25.426
A refund issued for a payment that actually failed (or a release for a confirmed order), or a retry without a key that charges twice (L3:

1022
01:10:25.706 --> 01:10:27.093
141).

1023
01:10:27.373 --> 01:10:28.098
Fix:

1024
01:10:28.378 --> 01:10:29.957
Treat timeouts as unknown.

1025
01:10:30.237 --> 01:10:33.522
Retry with the same idempotency key, and reconcile.

1026
01:10:34.872 --> 01:10:35.640
5.

1027
01:10:35.920 --> 01:10:37.883
Saga state kept only in memory.

1028
01:10:38.163 --> 01:10:38.973
Symptom:

1029
01:10:39.253 --> 01:10:43.648
A pod restart leaves checkouts half done, with holds and captures orphaned.

1030
01:10:43.928 --> 01:10:44.653
Fix:

1031
01:10:44.933 --> 01:10:48.112
Persist state per transition with conditional updates.

1032
01:10:48.392 --> 01:10:49.821
Run a recovery worker.

1033
01:10:50.101 --> 01:10:50.848
6.

1034
01:10:51.128 --> 01:10:53.923
Compensations that restore a previous value.

1035
01:10:55.273 --> 01:11:08.478
Here is the SQL code. before: undo by writing the old value; overwrites what other sagas did meanwhile (lost update). after: commutative inverse of the forward step, guarded so it happens once.

1036
01:11:11.328 --> 01:11:12.075
7.

1037
01:11:12.355 --> 01:11:14.552
Unguarded confirm versus expiry.

1038
01:11:14.832 --> 01:11:15.643
Symptom:

1039
01:11:15.923 --> 01:11:18.056
Oversold flash sale (L4:

1040
01:11:18.336 --> 01:11:20.363
801 for 500).

1041
01:11:20.643 --> 01:11:25.955
Fix: where status = 'HELD' and expiresat clocktimestamp() in the confirm itself.

1042
01:11:26.235 --> 01:11:26.917
8.

1043
01:11:27.197 --> 01:11:30.355
2PC or XA across microservices.

1044
01:11:30.635 --> 01:11:31.445
Symptom:

1045
01:11:31.725 --> 01:11:39.747
A coordinator restart blocks rows for minutes (lab 1: locks survived a server restart), and availability multiplies down.

1046
01:11:40.027 --> 01:11:40.752
Fix:

1047
01:11:41.032 --> 01:11:41.928
Sagas.

1048
01:11:42.208 --> 01:11:46.261
Keep 2PC inside one database product or trust domain.

1049
01:11:47.611 --> 01:11:48.358
9.

1050
01:11:48.638 --> 01:11:50.665
Choreography for a complex flow.

1051
01:11:50.945 --> 01:11:51.755
Symptom:

1052
01:11:52.035 --> 01:11:54.169
Nobody can answer where is order X?.

1053
01:11:54.449 --> 01:11:59.099
Compensations fire in the wrong order, and there are cyclic event dependencies.

1054
01:11:59.379 --> 01:12:00.105
Fix:

1055
01:12:00.385 --> 01:12:03.926
An orchestrator for flows with ordering and compensations.

1056
01:12:04.206 --> 01:12:05.422
Events for fan-out.

1057
01:12:05.702 --> 01:12:06.406
10.

1058
01:12:06.686 --> 01:12:10.825
Using CDC of internal tables as the public event contract.

1059
01:12:11.105 --> 01:12:11.915
Symptom:

1060
01:12:12.195 --> 01:12:14.478
A column rename breaks five consumers.

1061
01:12:14.758 --> 01:12:15.483
Fix:

1062
01:12:15.763 --> 01:12:20.414
